# Reawakening OS - the graphical application store.
#
# Round 16 replaces DDE Store with GNOME Software 48 and its Flatpak plugin.
# The store is Flatpak-first: Flathub is configured system-wide, and the same
# window can still install Debian packages through its APT plugin, so the
# traditional package manager stays useful for anyone who wants it.
#
# dde-store is intentionally gone from this list. It was a Qt 5 / DTK front end
# that crashed without a local patch, needed a light palette in a dark desktop
# and showed no application artwork. Its packaging stays in the repository so
# r15 can be rebuilt, but no shipping image carries it any more.
gnome-software
# The Flatpak backend. Without this package gnome-software only knows about
# Debian packages, which is precisely not what this round asked for.
gnome-software-plugin-flatpak
# flatpak itself, plus the D-Bus activated flatpak-system-helper that performs
# a system-wide install after polkit says yes. No daemon runs at boot.
flatpak
# Portals: Flatpak applications need xdg-desktop-portal for file dialogs and
# settings. The GTK backend is the one that works under labwc; it is a D-Bus
# service, started on demand and gone when idle.
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
# AppStream: the Debian package catalogue. appstreamcli builds
# /var/cache/swcatalog during the image build (see 0450-store).
appstream
# PackageKit and its APT backend (libpk_backend_apt.so). D-Bus activated, no
# [Install] section, exits after its idle timeout.
packagekit
# pkcon, the PackageKit diagnostic. 108 KiB, no daemon of its own, and the
# answer to "is the install path working at all?" without opening the store.
packagekit-tools
# The polkit authentication agent. Flatpak and PackageKit both ask polkitd for
# the administrator password; without a registered agent the request fails with
# "No authentication agent found" and nothing can be installed. mate-polkit
# reuses the GTK 3 stack the image already has (nm-connection-editor) and costs
# 68 KiB.
mate-polkit
# pkexec: runs the Cockpit remote-access helper through that same agent, so
# Settings -> Remote can ask for a password without a terminal.
pkexec
# wl-copy: the "Copy" button next to the Cockpit address in Settings -> Remote.
wl-clipboard
